1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,432
Accounting now runs on AI, automation, and blockchain.

2
00:00:04,482 --> 00:00:09,300
The accountant is no longer just a record keeper, but an analyst and advisor.

3
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:13,567
So, does learning with technology build more than technical skills?

4
00:00:15,617 --> 00:00:19,698
Employers see a gap between the skills they need and what graduates bring.

5
00:00:19,748 --> 00:00:24,542
Many programs still lean on theory, with limited hands-on use of digital tools.

6
00:00:24,592 --> 00:00:29,389
But past studies haven't shown how this technology actually builds competencies.

7
00:00:29,839 --> 00:00:37,149
Our study is anchored on Kolb's Experiential Learning, Siemens' Connectivism, and Bandura's Social Cognitive Theory.

8
00:00:37,599 --> 00:00:45,035
An Input, Process, Output model links respondents and core competencies to evidence-based policy recommendations.

9
00:00:45,485 --> 00:00:52,733
We ask newly passed CPAs how technology shaped five competencies from the International Education Standards:

10
00:00:52,783 --> 00:00:57,548
intellectual, technical, personal, interpersonal, and organizational skills.

11
00:00:58,598 --> 00:01:04,099
Is there a significant relationship? Our null hypothesis says no. The data will decide.

12
00:01:04,549 --> 00:01:08,988
We use a mixed-methods, nested design: a survey first, then interviews.

13
00:01:10,438 --> 00:01:17,306
From 112 newly passed CPAs from PLV, Slovin's formula sets a sample of at least 88.

14
00:01:17,356 --> 00:01:23,662
All passed the board exam from 2023 to 2025, and work in accounting.

15
00:01:24,112 --> 00:01:29,318
They answer a validated, four-point Likert survey, and ten join in-depth interviews.

16
00:01:29,768 --> 00:01:34,829
Weighted means, correlation, and thematic analysis turn their answers into insight.

17
00:01:35,879 --> 00:01:41,220
Participation is voluntary, and all data is protected under the Data Privacy Act.

18
00:01:41,670 --> 00:01:49,231
The findings will help CPAs, students, educators, and PLV shape an education that keeps pace with technology.

19
00:01:49,681 --> 00:01:53,561
Because the accountant of the future needs more than technical skills.

